# What shellcheck is told about this repository.
#
# SC2034 is the shadow of one file. Every script of this repository opens with
# the same cli template - the colour variables, the SCRIPT_DIR_PATH, the args
# array - and shellcheck sees 94 copies of it, so it reported 925 unused
# variables out of the 981 things it had to say about the repository. SC2034 is
# a warning, so it is the one of these that decides whether the job is red, and
# left on, the thirty three findings that are about the scripts themselves can
# not be found in the noise. A check nobody reads is not a check.
#
# SC2329 - print_usage and cleanup are never invoked - is 23 of the remaining
# 56 and is an info, so the job never saw it: --severity=warning had already
# dropped it. It is turned off for the person who runs "shellcheck a-script.sh"
# by hand, where no severity is passed and the same noise comes back.
#
# They are disabled here rather than with a directive in each file, because what
# is being described is the template rather than any one script that carries it.
#
# The vfio-pci scripts source a file that sits beside them, by a path that
# carries a variable. source-path is where to look for it and external-sources
# is permission to read it at all: without the second, shellcheck follows a
# sourced file only when that file happens to be one of the files it was asked
# to check. That is true of the job, which passes every script at once, and not
# of a run against one script, and the two would otherwise disagree about what
# the common file declares.
disable=SC2034
disable=SC2329
source-path=SCRIPTDIR
external-sources=true
